{
  "case_id": "2016-16-341",
  "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Monday, March 27, 2017\nThe above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How can that be when in Brunette we said that 1391 governed aliens, the definition of aliens?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It rests importantly on the \"except\" provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you don't have a venue statute like Section 1400, you get the kind of litigation experiences that are set out in the amici briefs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dabney",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DABNEY: Well, I -- I would -- I would respectfully disagree because what 1400(b) does is it provides a different way to define venue for nonresident defendants. 1400(b) isn't restricted just to the district where the defendant is domiciled. 1400(b) provides not the expansive regime that 1391(c) does, you know, anyplace where, you know, someone could constitutionally summon you into court. 1400(b) says you have to have a regular and established place of business and commit an act of infringement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Now, as long as you have a minute, maybe you could indulge me and trace me through this. With a corporation, I think 1400 says resides, where the defendant resides."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JAY: Fourco -- the principles by which Fourco interpret the statutes are still good law --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But, Mr. Jay, can I just ask you -- and this is a clarification question, and maybe I should know this. But you have the original 1391, which was the subject of Fourco."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jay",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JAY: It wasn't because now it's no longer just corporate defendants. The 2011 amendment adds to the definition. It provides for a domicile for individual defendants. It expands the (c)(2) definition to cover other business entities besides corporations, which wasn't done in the '88 amendment, and it provides a rule that slightly tweaks what this Court said in Brunette."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: You asked me this"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alderson Reporting Company",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You can sue a defendant in the judicial district where his domicile is, or if you want to sue somewhere else, you have to sue somewhere where there is both an act of infringement and a regular established place of business."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alderson Reporting Company",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So those are the only kind of actions that 1400(b) applies to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Alderson Reporting Company",
      "case_id": "2016-16-341",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "bf4dc16b57aea93195b33d79772ed701c6c282e103df677fad450864a9dbc2e7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bf4dc16b57ae-0003-0002",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that paper cited on page 52 indicates that 68 percent of small- and medium-sized businesses will get venue relief if TC Heartland wins this case."
    },
    {
